    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18015553/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a9e1-79d7936f7408": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (Outbound Services)",
      "description": "Assistant Manager (Outbound Services) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Assistant Manager (Outbound Services) Fixed Terms Closing on 01 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Assistant Manager, Outbound Services, will drive process improvement and digital enablement for the administration of student overseas programmes. The role will review end-to-end workflows, translate operational needs into system requirements, coordinate enhancements to the SP Overseas Programme system module and related platforms, conduct data validation and user acceptance testing, and support implementation and user adoption. Working with Academic Schools, Departments and relevant stakeholders, the candidate will also oversee selected outbound operational processes to ensure that they are efficient, accurate, user-centred and compliant with requirements. What you will be working on Review and redesign end-to-end overseas programme workflows to address pain points and control gaps, and introduce opportunities for simplification, automation and self-service. Translate operational needs into functional requirements, coordinate system enhancements with colleagues in IT, and oversee user acceptance testing and implementation. Maintain operational documentation, monitor compliance, conduct user training and support the adoption of new processes and systems. Improve data quality and develop dashboards and reports to support operational monitoring and management decision-making. Oversee selected overseas programme processes, including trip submissions, insurance, funding, procurement, stakeholder enquiries and exception management. What we are looking for Relevant diploma or degree in Information Technology, Information Systems, Computer Science or a related discipline; relevant professional certifications would be advantageous. 2 – 4 years of relevant experience in business analysis, systems implementation, digital transformation, process improvement, project management or operations, preferably in the public sector. Strong process-mapping and business-analysis skills, with experience in requirements gathering, system enhancements, user acceptance testing and implementation. Proficiency in digital tools, data analysis and reporting; familiarity with Microsoft 365, Power BI and low-code automation tools would be advantageous. Strong project-management, stakeholder-engagement, communication and documentation skills, with an analytical, detail-oriented and service-focused approach. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 01 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17994918/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a8e3-c632a8513406": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Technology & Analytics",
      "description": "Lecturer, Technology & Analytics - School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer, Technology & Analytics - School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging but meaningful. Not only will s/he have both the knowledge and working experience, s/he must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/ Institutional strategic initiatives will also be an important part of the job. The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on As a lecturer in the School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics, you will be primarily responsible for teaching in the domain of Technology and Analytics , with a focus on areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Data Analytics, Data Visualisation, and Quantum Computing. You will also be expected to teach in at least one complementary area such as Mathematics, Statistics, or Programming. In line with SP's Common Core Curriculum, you will also be expected to teach at least one interdisciplinary module, which may include: Data Fluency Artificial Intelligence & Its Impact Persuasive Communication with Data Storytelling Problem Solving with Creative and Computational Thinking Beyond the classroom, you will play an active role in shaping and evolving the curriculum. This includes: Developing and reviewing course materials and assessments to enhance student learning, performance, and employability Staying current with trends and developments in Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Data Analytics, Data Visualisation, and Quantum Computing to ensure the curriculum remains relevant and up to date Undertaking project and consultancy work with internal and external stakeholders, applying your expertise in real-world contexts What we are looking for Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team Relevant qualification in Mathematics, Statistics, Physics or Engineering Relevant industry experience and/or knowledge of how statistics is applied in different fields such as Data Analytics, Engineering or IT People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skill Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17994914/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a8e3-c56296709406": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Mathematics",
      "description": "Lecturer, Mathematics - School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer, Mathematics - School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging but meaningful. Not only will s/he have both the knowledge and working experience, s/he must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/ Institutional strategic initiatives will also be an important part of the job. The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on As a lecturer in the School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics, you will be primarily responsible for teaching Mathematics , with the ability to also teach in at least one complementary area such as Statistics, Data Analytics, Programming, or IT applications (e.g. Excel). In line with SP's Common Core Curriculum, you will also be expected to teach at least one interdisciplinary module, which may include: Data Fluency Artificial Intelligence & Its Impact Persuasive Communication with Data Storytelling Problem Solving with Creative and Computational Thinking Beyond the classroom, you will play an active role in shaping and evolving the curriculum. This includes: Developing and reviewing course materials and assessments to enhance student learning, performance, and employability Staying current with trends and developments in Mathematics to ensure the curriculum remains relevant and up to date Designing new class activities and contributing to pedagogical innovation to enrich the student learning experience What we are looking for Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team Relevant qualification in Mathematics, Statistics, Physics or Engineering Relevant industry experience and/or knowledge of how mathematics is applied in different fields such as Engineering, IT or Data Analytics People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skill Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
