    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17842874/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a7ff-27e62f6b7405": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Software & Applications)",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Software & Applications) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Software & Applications) Fixed Terms Closing on 23 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will they have both the knowledge and working experience, but they must also possess the ability to deconstruct the knowledge and experience, guiding students to reconstruct them as their own knowledge. He/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop the curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on Software and Applications The appointee must be competent to teach in at least one of the following subjects: Algorithm & Architecture Analysis – A good understanding of tools, frameworks, and language paradigms to make informed decisions about chosen implementations and their trade-offs on performance, such as time/space complexity, resource utilization, and system scalability. Database Systems – A good understanding of database performance optimization through techniques such as sharding, indexing, query tuning, concurrency, and the handling of distributed transactions. Distributed Systems – A good understanding of modern architectural patterns and system components—such as microservices, containerization, load balancing, and message queues—and how to integrate them to build reliable, scalable, and fault-tolerant infrastructure. Apart from the know-hows of the tools and processes, the lecturer should possess clear understanding of the end-to-end process of software development, facilitating students in the deconstruction and reconstruction of concepts, analysing the trade-offs, and explaining how different companies may adopt a slightly different configuration from another. Responsibilities:- Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning of students (youths and adult learners) Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum.  This includes regular review of existing curriculum and make recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ learning, performance and employability. Keep current and abreast of trends and developments of Software and Application Development. Support the School’ strategic initiatives through involvement in committee work and projects such as process improvement projects, development and management of new courses What we are looking for Requirements:- Minimum 2 years of relevant work experience in Software/DevOps/Platform/Database engineering. Passionate about tinkering and hacking to gain understanding of the underlying mechanisms of things. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in guiding youths and adult learners in deconstructing and reconstructing knowledge. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 23 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17979532/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a7ff-2af38121d405": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Events & Business Development",
      "description": "Assistant Manager, Events & Business Development - Industry & Partnerships | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Assistant Manager, Events & Business Development - Industry & Partnerships Fixed Terms Closing on 22 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Assistant Manager, Events & Business Development in the Department of Industry & Partnerships (INP) leads the end-to-end management of corporate and industry events, ensuring alignment with organisational goals. This role manages complex event logistics, including event flow, attendee experience, vendor coordination, and contingency planning. The role also leads industry workforce transformation and advisory initiatives. This includes engaging companies to identify business and workforce capability gaps, developing skills maps and future-ready workforce plans, and advising on upskilling, reskilling, and job redesign strategies aligned with national frameworks such as SkillsFuture. The role will require strong coordination skills, sound judgement, good business acumen and the ability to manage multiple platforms, stakeholders, and deliverables independently. What you will be working on Key Responsibilities: Events & Campaigns (Industry Engagement) Support the planning and delivery of marketing and communications for major industry events, conferences, exhibitions, and summits. Coordinate event-related communications including key messages, programmes, stage content, signage, media materials, multimedia assets, and post-event highlights. Work closely with internal teams, partners, vendors, and organisers to ensure consistency and accuracy of messaging across event touchpoints. Support post-event reporting, content curation, and documentation to evaluate impact and inform future improvements. Business Development Curate and customise industry-relevant training packages by translating company needs into structured learning journeys, leveraging Singapore Polytechnic’s short courses and modular programmes. Develop and deliver company-specific competency and skills roadmaps by mapping current and future skill requirements against job roles and business objectives, and recommending progressive upskilling pathways leveraging Singapore Polytechnic’s CET offerings. Lead and deliver industry workforce transformation and advisory initiatives by engaging companies to diagnose business and workforce capability gaps What we are looking for Requirements: Degree in Events Management, Communications, Marketing, Business Development, Business, or a related discipline. Minimum 4 to 6 years of relevant experience in Events Management and Business Development. Experience in public sector, education, or large organisations is an advantage. Experience working with senior stakeholders and cross-functional teams. Strong planning and coordination skills in complex event management. Good stakeholder management. Strong organisational and project management abilities. Able to work independently, prioritise tasks, and manage ambiguity. Professional, grounded, and people-oriented. Detail-oriented with a strong sense of responsibility and follow-through. Able to remain calm under pressure and manage competing priorities. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 22 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17964610/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a781-70e3ff1922b4": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning) - School of Business | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning) - School of Business Fixed Terms Closing on 17 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 At the Singapore Polytechnic School of Business, we believe in creating engaging and meaningful learning experiences that develop students' critical thinking, creativity, adaptability and problem-solving skills. Through applied and experiential learning, students are given opportunities to connect classroom learning with real-world business contexts and develop the confidence to take initiative and respond to new challenges. This is a hands-on academic role with a strong focus on student development, programme delivery and teaching. We are looking for someone who enjoys working with youths and is comfortable taking an active role both in and beyond the classroom. A key part of the role is to lead, plan and execute student development and entrepreneurship-related programmes, events, learning journeys, overseas programmes and other school initiatives. The appointee should be organised, adaptable, resourceful and able to take ownership of programmes from planning through to delivery, including coordinating students, colleagues, industry partners and other stakeholders, as well as managing the necessary logistics and administrative arrangements. The appointee must be competent and comfortable teaching in at least one of the following subject areas. Prior teaching experience would be advantageous: •\tBusiness foundation modules such as Marketing, Human Resource Management or Business Negotiation •\tEntrepreneurship or Innovation-related modules What you will be working on Responsibilities: Lead, plan, coordinate and execute school programmes, events, student development activities, entrepreneurship-related initiatives, learning journeys and overseas programmes, including managing the necessary logistics, budgeting, administration, documentation and coordination with internal and external stakeholders. Deliver and administer assigned modules, including teaching, learning activities and assessments. Provide pastoral care, guidance and support to students. What we are looking for Requirements: Minimum 2 years of relevant working experience and/or professional experience. Relevant qualification in Business, Entrepreneurship, Innovation or a related discipline. Strong interest in teaching and working with students, with genuine concern for their learning, development and well-being. Self-driven, adaptable and resourceful, with good time-management and problem-solving skills. Organised, responsible and able to manage multiple teaching and programme-related responsibilities. Strong team player with good interpersonal and communication skills. Experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, start-ups or the innovation ecosystem would be an advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 17 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17960724/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a6e8-4c321abb42b1": {
      "title": "Lead Technical Executive, Facilities Management",
      "description": "Lead Technical Executive, Facilities Management - Dept of Estates & Development | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lead Technical Executive, Facilities Management - Dept of Estates & Development Fixed Terms Closing on 17 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 This role supports Singapore Polytechnic’s Facilities and Assets Management function by managing and improving Facilities Management (FM) services, maintenance programmes, operational contracts and campus facilities initiatives. The candidate works with schools, departments, consultants, contractors and service providers to deliver safe, effective and compliant facilities services and maintenance programmes, covering procurement, contract management, operational problem-solving, A&A and facilities improvement projects. The candidate applies professional knowledge and sound judgement to resolve operational and maintenance issues, improve service delivery, asset performance and efficiency, communicate effectively with stakeholders, and coordinate multiple initiatives and projects. What you will be working on You will be responsible for the following: Facilities Maintenance and Project Administration Support Singapore Polytechnic’s Facilities and Assets Management matters, including the coordination and administration of landscape maintenance, pest control, carpark operations, facilities improvement works, projects, procurement and tender administration, as well as the management of SP-appointed FM contractors, service providers and carpark operators. Manage and administer FM services, maintenance programmes and operational contracts to support safe, reliable and effective campus operations. Plan, organise and coordinate maintenance activities, facilities services, A&A works and improvement projects to meet operational and user requirements. Oversee contractors, consultants and service providers to ensure works and services are delivered in accordance with contract specifications, service standards, safety requirements and regulatory requirements. Coordinate with schools, departments, users and stakeholders to address maintenance needs, service concerns, operational issues and project requirements. Conduct site inspections, audits, investigations and performance reviews to monitor service quality, contractor performance, compliance and areas for improvement. Administer maintenance contracts and project matters, including scope definition, budgeting, procurement support, approvals, records, variation orders, claims, implementation and close-out. Monitor project schedules, milestones, risks, deliverables, budgets and expenditure to ensure timely, safe and cost-effective completion of works. Prepare and maintain management papers, reports, presentations, procurement submissions, project documentation and other records in accordance with SP policies and procedures. Provide operational and technical inputs in meetings, maintenance reviews, service performance discussions and project coordination sessions. Identify and support service, maintenance, asset and process improvement initiatives to enhance operational efficiency, service quality and campus user experience. Keep abreast of relevant industry practices, emerging technologies, Singapore Standards and regulatory requirements relating to facilities management, building maintenance and service delivery. Support departmental initiatives and contribute to continuous improvement in facilities management, asset management and operational excellence. Other Programme Management and Strategic Initiatives Manage and coordinate multiple operational initiatives, facilities improvement projects and departmental programmes concurrently. Support digitalisation, sustainability, reliability and asset lifecycle management initiatives where required. Undertake any other duties and responsibilities as assigned. What we are looking for Requirements Qualification Required and Area of Discipline. Minimum diploma or degree in Facilities Management, Estate Management, Project Management (or related discipline). Minimum 5 years of relevant working experiences in facilities management, contract administration, operational services management or project management. Experience in managing FM services, operational contracts, procurement activities and contractor performance. Experience in tender preparation, procurement administration and contract management. Experience in Addition & Alteration (A&A), upgrading or facilities improvement projects. Knowledge and Skills Good understanding of facilities management principles, contract administration, operational service delivery, government procurement, regulatory requirements and legislation. Good analytical, critical thinking, coordination and project management skills, with the ability to assess operational issues and recommend practical solutions. Good communication, presentation, negotiation and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders at different levels and explain complex or sensitive matters clearly. Positive work attitude, good listening ability and ability to work collaboratively with staff at all levels as a reliable and independent team member. Good leadership qualities, strategic planning capabilities, time management, resourcefulness, self-motivation and ability to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently. Relevant professional certifications or experience in facilities management, sustainability (e.g. Green Mark Accredited Professional (GMAP) accreditation or equivalent), quality management, safety management, project management, Building Information Modelling (BIM), and tender specification preparation would be advantageous. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 17 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17940431/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a5d1-6f521049f402": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Academic Quality & Resources (FabLab)",
      "description": "Lecturer, Academic Quality & Resources (FabLab) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer, Academic Quality & Resources (FabLab) Fixed Terms Closing on 11 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore's first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is as a polytechnic for all ages, we prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready, and world ready for the transformation of Singapore. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. What you will be working on We are looking for an experienced and hands-on professional to join our FabLab team. In this role, you will develop and deliver applied learning in digital fabrication, electronics, programming and maker education, while supporting the safe, reliable and effective operation of SP FabLab. You will help students and partners translate ideas into functional prototypes through design, making, testing and iteration. Responsibilities 1. Teaching and Learner Development Plan and deliver engaging lessons, laboratory sessions and workshops in digital fabrication, programming, electronics and maker education. Facilitate hands-on learning experiences, supervise student projects, assess learning outcomes, and provide timely feedback to support learners' technical development and success. 2. Curriculum and Learning Resource Development Develop and enhance project-based curricula, lesson materials, assessments and learning resources that incorporate digital fabrication technologies, coding, electronics, design thinking and emerging technologies such as AI. Ensure that content remains current, industry-relevant and aligned with learner needs. 3. FabLab Operations, Technical Support and Safety Management Support the day-to-day operation of the FabLab by maintaining fabrication equipment, electronics prototyping tools and related software. Develop and implement safety procedures, conduct training, troubleshoot technical issues and support equipment maintenance to ensure a safe, reliable and effective learning environment. 4. Applied Projects, Industry Partnerships and Outreach Collaborate with industry, schools and community partners on applied projects and consultancy initiatives. Support prototype development, facilitate innovation projects, and contribute to outreach programmes, showcases and professional engagements that strengthen the impact and visibility of the FabLab. What we are looking for Requirements Essential Requirements Bachelor's degree in Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Computer Engineering, Mechatronics, Digital Fabrication, Industrial/Product Design, or a closely related discipline. At least 5 years of relevant industry, applied project and/or teaching experience, including experience in a tertiary, adult-learning or comparable technical learning environment. Hands-on experience across the design-to-fabrication workflow, including CAD/CAM and digital fabrication technologies such as 3D printing, laser cutting, CNC machining, electronics prototyping or related processes. Proficiency in programming and electronics prototyping using platforms such as Arduino, micro:bit, ESP32 or Raspberry Pi, together with programming languages such as Python or C/C++. Ability to design and deliver project-based, studio or laboratory learning, including the development of lesson plans, assessments and learning resources. Strong knowledge of workshop or laboratory safety practices, risk assessment, SOP development, equipment maintenance and technical troubleshooting. Excellent communication, facilitation and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts clearly and work effectively across multidisciplinary teams. Preferred Requirements Postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline. Knowledge or experience in product design, industrial design, design thinking, user-centred design or product prototyping. A portfolio demonstrating completed prototypes, applied projects, teaching innovations or related work. Teaching or facilitation qualifications such as ACTA, ACLP or equivalent. Relevant industry certifications, consultancy experience, or active participation in maker, fabrication or innovation communities. Candidates should be prepared to present a technical portfolio and may be required to complete a teaching demonstration and/or practical technical assessment as part of the selection process. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 11 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17935414/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a5b8-4a778dde22ad": {
      "title": "Technical Executive",
      "description": "Technical Executive - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Technical Executive - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026. The appointee must have good interpersonal skills, willing to learn on the job and be a team player. He/She must undertake duties that support the smooth functioning of the School and School’s labs, provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. What you will be working on Responsibilities: •    Provide technical assistance and support for lab operations •    Ensure Staff and students adhere to safety procedures and be properly attired •    Ensure that equipment and machines are in working order and are safe for operations •    Planning and ordering of raw materials for Lab/FYP use •    Liaise with Estates Dept for related service request pertaining to lab facilities •    Attend to asset management activities including asset write off and disposal, asset verification, storage •    Planning for machine and equipment maintenance Requirements: •    Tertiary qualification in Mechanical/Electrical Engineering •    2-3 years' hands-on experiences working in the Mechanical Engineering - Materials and Testing Industry. Examples include Tensile test, Impact test, NDT and Heat Treatment. •    Fresh graduates are welcomed to apply. What we are looking for Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
