    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17935417/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a5b8-4b544671c2ad": {
      "title": "Technical Executive",
      "description": "Technical Executive - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Technical Executive - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The appointee must have good interpersonal skills, willing to learn on the job and be a team player. He/she must undertake duties that support the smooth functioning of the School and School’s labs, provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. What you will be working on Responsibilities: Provided technical assistance and support for lab with regards to ARVR Projects and other labs in the AeroHub and support consultancy projects. Ensure Staff and students adhere to safety procedures, and have proper attire. Support/Assist/Conduct lab experiments for both PET and CET courses. Ensure that equipment and machines are in working order safe for operations. Planning and Ordering of raw materials if required for Lab/FYP use. Contact Estates for related service request pertaining to lab facilities Attend to asset management activities. i.e write off, asset verification, storage. Planning for machine and equipment maintenance. What we are looking for Requirements: Tertiary qualification in Mechanical/Electrical/Computer Engineering. 2-3 years hands-on experiences working in the Mechanical Engineering Environment. Experiences in Programming, Unity, Blender, Adobe Creative Suite, app and website development. Fresh graduates are welcomed to apply. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
