    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/16993196/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a4d3-ae70289b42ad": {
      "title": "Lead (Continuing Education & Training)",
      "description": "Lead (Continuing Education & Training) - School of Computing | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lead (Continuing Education & Training) - School of Computing Fixed Terms Closing in 4  day(s) Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic and continuing education leader is challenging and meaningful. Beyond having strong educational and industry understanding, the appointee must possess a passion for lifelong learning, workforce upskilling and industry collaboration. The role involves leading Continuing Education & Training (CET) initiatives within the School of Computing, strengthening partnerships with employers and agencies. Successful candidates are expected to be resourceful, collaborative and forward-looking, with strong leadership, communication, stakeholder management and project delivery skills. What you will be working on Continuing Education & Training Leadership and Industry Engagement The appointee will lead and coordinate CET initiatives within the School of Computing, working closely with academic teams, PACE, industry partners, alumni and external agencies to develop relevant programmes, strengthen learner outreach and support Singapore’s continuing education and workforce transformation needs. Responsibilities: Lead and oversee CET functional areas within the School of Computing, including CET planning, programme operations and achievement of school-level CET targets. Drive the development, launch and continuous review of market-responsive CET programmes, including part-time diplomas, specialist diplomas, Work-Study Programmes, SCTP, short courses and modular training. Strengthen industry engagement, plan & execute outreach initiatives and key account management by identifying collaboration opportunities and maintaining effective relationships with industry partners. Contribute to school-level strategic initiatives, including alumni collaboration, industry projects, staff capability development and the growth of new computing-related CET domains. What we are looking for Requirements: Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in continuing education and training, adult learning, programme management, industry engagement, business development, academic administration or related areas. Proven ability to lead projects, coordinate cross-functional teams, manage stakeholders and deliver outcomes within agreed timelines. Self-driven, resourceful and able to work collaboratively across teams and stakeholders. Knowledge of IT, computing or digital transformation areas such as artificial intelligence, data analytics, software development, cloud, cybersecurity, automation or low-code platforms would be a plus. Preferably able to develop content and curriculum in emerging AI areas. Relevant qualification in Computing, Information Technology, Education, Business, Management or related disciplines. Postgraduate qualifications, adult education credentials or relevant professional certifications would be an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing in 4  day(s). If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17912291/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a488-471cc57b02ad": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) - School of ABE | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) - School of ABE Fixed Terms Closing in 2  day(s) Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. The role of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only does he/she need to have domain knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them and molding their characters. The job offers opportunities for curriculum and pedagogical development, as well as industry engagements in the form of consultancy or applied research. Administrative work related to teaching and school/institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful, innovative and articulate. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) The appointee must be competent to teach in the following key areas of the Construction Industry Transformation Map (ITM) and architectural domains at diploma level: •\tIntegrated Digital Delivery (IDD), with a focus on Computational Design and A.I. applications •\tArchitectural Design •\tHistory and Theory of Architecture •\tEnvironmental Science •\tGreen Buildings •\tMaterials and Technology •\tDesign for Manufacturing & Assembly (DfMA) What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students with an emphasis on Computational Design, A.I. applications and History and Theory of Architecture. Keep abreast of current developments and trends in the areas of the Construction Industry Transformation Map and/or Architectural domains to develop and maintain relevant and up-to-date teaching curriculum. This includes review of existing curriculum with a view to making recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ performance, learning & employability. Enhance students’ learning through other activities such as training students for competitions, supervising projects and internships, and leading them on overseas learning program/community service. Collaborate with other staff as well as industry to offer meaningful applied industry projects and consultancy projects.  Support SkillsFuture initiatives in the implementation of Enhanced Internship Programmes, Work Study Programme and CET programmes. What we are looking for Requirements: Possess relevant qualifications and professional certifications in Architecture, with at least 4 years of relevant experience, preferably in Computational Design and AI applications. Demonstrate strong knowledge of Architectural History and Theory from the 1900s onwards. Exhibit a passion for teaching, knowledge-sharing, and mentoring students and adult learners. Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills, and work effectively as a team player. Ability to engage industry partners and contribute to consultancy projects. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing in 2  day(s). If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17005743/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a898-6129b34f42b9": {
      "title": "Technical Executive",
      "description": "Technical Executive - School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Technical Executive - School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 24 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. For this position, the appointee will be part of the lab management team that supports the smooth functioning of the school’s labs and to provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising/guiding students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. Besides lab management, the appointee also has the opportunity to provide administrative and technical support to ensure smooth operation of key functional and/or project works related to the various initiatives carried out by the school. What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Support the smooth functioning of the school’s labs and assisting/conducting of lab experiments for both PET and CET courses. Provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising/guiding students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. Undertake project/consultancy work with both internal and external stakeholders Manage stock inventory and acquire all resources necessary for the laboratories and yearly budgeting for teaching material and equipment maintenance. To liaise with vendors and evaluate quotations from suppliers for purchasing materials and lab equipment To support and assist to troubleshoot electrical/electronic/IT systems and effect minor repairs of faulty equipment of the lab facilities where necessary To housekeep lab facilities by carrying out regular lab maintenance and ensure the safety of the labs according to safety guidelines. To provide support which include coordination, consultation with various stakeholders, follow-up and implementation in school functional and/or project work. What we are looking for General Requirements:- Tertiary qualification in Electronic/Computer Engineering, or equivalent qualification in a related discipline. At least 2 years' hands-on experience working on Engineering projects. Candidates with at least 2 years of relevant working experience in one of the areas below would have an added advantage: (a) Electronics Design and Development (b) Embedded Systems (c) Computer Networking Self-driven, possess good interpersonal skills, willing to learn on the job and be a team player. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 24 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17809532/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a8b1-717625af82bb": {
      "title": "Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning",
      "description": "Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning - Dept of Student Development | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning - Dept of Student Development Fixed Terms Closing on 25 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Department of Student Development (SD) provides all SP students with a positive Polytechnic experience through meaningful out-of-classroom activities that support holistic student development. As an Assistant Manager/Deputy Manager, the appointee will initiate and lead programmes within the Service-Learning portfolio in the Department of Student Development, with the aim of developing students' social responsibility, character, leadership and community engagement through meaningful service-learning experiences. He/she will be supporting the strategic directives for Service-Learning with involvement in programme planning, stakeholder engagement, communications and conducting relevant data analysis for tracking and continuous improvement. The role will also include mentoring/guiding students in Co-Curricular Activities (CCA) club matters. He/she may be required to collaborate with diverse stakeholders to organise SP-wide events that enhance campus vibrancy and participate in departmental committees. What you will be working on a) Design and lead service-learning and sustainability programmes and activities, ensuring objectives are achieved: Coordinate programme execution, logistics and stakeholder engagement Conduct data tracking, analysis and reporting for continuous improvement Manage programme administration, budgets and vendors (where applicable) Support communications and outreach for programmes and initiatives b) Develop and maintain partnerships with diverse stakeholders to lead meaningful service-learning and sustainability programmes and opportunities. c) Mentor and guide students in CCA clubs, including leadership development and administrative support. d) Support departmental administrative processes and perform ad-hoc duties as assigned. What we are looking for Passion for student/youth development. Minimum 2 years’ experience in service-learning, youth development, education or related fields. Strong organisational, administrative and analytical skills. Good interpersonal, communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Self-motivated, proactive and able to work independently as well as collaboratively. Willing to work beyond office hours when required. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 25 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17340789/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a5ea-98af79a7d402": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer - School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 12 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will he/she has both the knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing and moulding their characters. The successful candidate will be expected to play a critical role in curriculum development, pedagogy innovation and participation in applied research projects.  There will be opportunities to introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job.  The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on Responsibilities: - Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials and mentoring of students Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum modules Undertake projects/consultancy work with both internal and external stakeholders Deploy effective pedagogy to facilitate learning General Requirements: - Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team People-oriented individuals with strong interpersonal, written and communication skills Candidates who possess experience in teaching will have an added advantage Keen interest to develop new capabilities through projects and self-learning Possess strong interest in exploring new technologies Contribute to the teaching of the Professional Adult and Continuing Education (PACE) classes conducted at night. What we are looking for Additional Requirements (Lecturer –Cybersecurity and Networking): Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: Firewall Technology Cloud Computing Cyber Security Possess 3 years of relevant working experiences in one of the above areas. Candidates with experience with industrial and applied experience, e.g. Data Analytics, Machine Learning and AI applied to manufacturing or other engineering settings, Industry Control Systems/Operation Technology Security, would be an added advantage. Additional Requirements (Lecturer – Aerospace): - Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: (a) Aircraft electrical and electronics systems (b) Aviation Cybersecurity (c) Drone Technologies Possess 3 years of relevant working experience in one of the above areas. Candidates with experience in AI applications for aerospace and/or IoT integration in aircraft systems will have an added advantage. Additional Requirements (Lecturer –Power and Sustainable Energy): - Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: (a) Building Energy Efficiency & Management (b) Electrical Power systems & Installation (c) Power Electronics & Drives (d) Energy Storage Systems Possess 3 years of relevant work experience in one of the above areas Candidate who is currently a Professional Engineer (PE) or in the process of becoming a PE would have an added advantage. Additional Requirements (Lecturer –Industrial Control, Automation and Robotics): - Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: (a) Automation System Integration (b) Industrial Robotics and Autonomous Systems (c) Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) (d) Embodied AI Possess 3 years of relevant work experience in one of the above areas Candidate with industrial robotics, AMRs, ROS2, machine vision, embodied AI, human-robot interaction, AIoT, industrial cybersecurity, and systems integration will be an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17659201/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a8e3-c6574514f406": {
      "title": "Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics",
      "description": "Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging but meaningful. Not only will s/he have both the knowledge and working experience, s/he must also possess a passion for working with youths and adult learners. There will be opportunities to develop curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and applied industry/research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/ Institutional strategic initiatives will also be an important part of the job. The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on As a lecturer in the School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics, you will be primarily responsible for teaching in the domain of Data Science & Artificial Intelligence , with a focus on at least one of the following areas: Artificial Intelligence (AI) Computer Vision (CV) Data Science (DS) Data Analytics (DA) Natural Language Processing (NLP) You will also be expected to teach in at least one complementary area such as Mathematics, Statistics, or Computing. In line with SP's Common Core Curriculum, you will also be expected to teach at least one interdisciplinary module, which may include: Data Fluency Artificial Intelligence & Its Impact Persuasive Communication with Data Storytelling Problem Solving with Creative and Computational Thinking Beyond the classroom, you will play an active role in shaping and evolving the curriculum. This includes: Developing and reviewing course materials and assessments to enhance student learning, performance, and employability Staying current with trends and developments in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, Data Science, Data Analytics, and Natural Language Processing to ensure the curriculum remains relevant and up to date Undertaking project and consultancy work with internal and external stakeholders, applying your expertise in real-world contexts What we are looking for Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team Relevant qualification in Mathematics, Statistics, Physics or Engineering Relevant industry experience and/or knowledge of how statistics is applied in different fields such as Data Analytics, Engineering or IT People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skill Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
